# Brenz base architecture

Source: `@docs/architecture/brenz-architecture-base.md`.

## Rules
- Target iOS 17 as the minimum.
- Use MVVM with `@Observable @MainActor final class` for every ViewModel.
- Create repositories and use cases only in `AppContainer`. Inject it through `Environment` from `BrenzApp`.
- Pass use cases to ViewModels through the initializer.
- Organize by layer: `App/`, `Core/`, `Domain/`, `Data/`, `Presentation/`, `Resources/`.
- Inside `Domain/`: `Entities/`, `Rules/`, `UseCases/`, `Repositories/` (protocols only).
- Inside `Data/`: `Firebase/` and `Local/`.
- Put views that use entities and are shared across features in `Presentation/Shared/`.
- Add Firebase only through Swift Package Manager: `FirebaseAuth`, `FirebaseFirestore`, `FirebaseRemoteConfig`.
- Use `os.Logger`, one `Logger` per layer, without email or nickname.
- Write tests with Swift Testing. Use fake repositories for Domain and ViewModels.
- Keep Firestore rules and emulator tests in `firebase/`.
- Write all visible text in `Localizable.xcstrings` (`en` base, `es`).
- Write code, identifiers, comments, file names and documentation in English.

## Forbidden
- Do not add third-party libraries (Factory, Swinject, TCA, Lottie, Analytics, Crashlytics).
- Do not use `Combine`.
- Do not create SPM modules per layer. The only exception is `Packages/BrenzDesignSystem/`.
- Do not import Firebase outside `Data/Firebase/`.
- Do not write visible text in code.
- Do not add UI tests in v1.
- Do not put theme or colors in `Core/`. They live in `BrenzDesignSystem`.
